From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] i18npool: do not crash when the saxparser output file cannot be opened

The build-host tool saxparser generates the localedata_*.cxx sources via
OFileWriter. Its constructor opens the output file with fopen() but never
checks the result, while every write method (writeAsciiString() and the
rest) does fprintf(m_f, ...) with no NULL check. When fopen() fails the
first write dereferences a NULL FILE* and the tool dies with a bare
"Segmentation fault (core dumped)", failing do_compile with no clue why.

fopen() fails transiently under a heavy parallel build: gbuild runs the
localedata generation with its own parallelism, so many saxparser run at
once and a signal interrupting the underlying open() surfaces as fopen()
returning NULL with errno == EINTR. The locale it dies on is therefore
non-deterministic and load-correlated. It is not a resource limit (checked
while failing: plenty of free space, file descriptors and inodes).

Retry fopen() on EINTR, and if it still fails print the file name and the
errno string and exit(1), so a genuine failure is reported instead of
crashing.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 i18npool/source/localedata/filewriter.cxx | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/i18npool/source/localedata/filewriter.cxx b/i18npool/source/localedata/filewriter.cxx
--- a/i18npool/source/localedata/filewriter.cxx
+++ b/i18npool/source/localedata/filewriter.cxx
@@ -18,6 +18,9 @@
  */

 #include <stdio.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
+#include <errno.h>
 #include "LocaleNode.hxx"

 // The document handler, which is needed for the saxparser
@@ -26,7 +29,19 @@
 OFileWriter::OFileWriter(const char *pcFile, const char *locale ): theLocale(locale) {

     printf("file generated=%s\n", pcFile);
-    m_f = fopen(pcFile, "w");
+    // fopen() can fail transiently under a heavy parallel build (e.g. EINTR
+    // from signal churn while many localedata generators run at once). Retry on
+    // EINTR, and if it still fails, abort with a clear message: every write
+    // method below does fprintf(m_f, ...) with no NULL check, so a NULL m_f
+    // would otherwise crash with a bare SIGSEGV that is hard to diagnose.
+    do {
+        m_f = fopen(pcFile, "w");
+    } while (m_f == nullptr && errno == EINTR);
+    if (m_f == nullptr) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "saxparser: cannot open output file '%s': %s\n",
+                pcFile, strerror(errno));
+        exit(1);
+    }
 }

 OFileWriter::~OFileWriter() {
